    {
      "id": "frag-11",
      "focal_uid": 11,
      "title": "Who pays for a century",
      "insight": "Sustained political will is what turns a healthy economy into an actual interstellar budget, and cheap access to orbit is what makes the sheer mass affordable. It lands on the arrival date directly and bankrolls the fusion work underneath it. The most mundane driver on the map is the one gating all the exotic ones.",
      "role": "driver",
