    {
      "id": "frag-2",
      "focal_uid": 2,
      "title": "The fuel that doesn't exist yet",
      "insight": "Antimatter is made today in nanograms; a crewed crossing would need kilograms. Fusion power and off-Earth industry are what could make that scale-up thinkable, and if it lands it feeds straight into relativistic propulsion - the difference between a decades-long crossing and one no crew could outlive.",
      "role": "driver",
      "importance": 86,
