    {
      "id": "frag-8",
      "focal_uid": 8,
      "title": "Going fast makes space lethal",
      "insight": "At a fifth of light speed a grain of interstellar dust arrives like a bomb, and cosmic rays never let up. Fusion power and the propulsion it feeds both raise the shielding bar, and shielding in turn decides whether the life-support loop is survivable at all. It sits between speed and survival.",
